Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::a_retyped_run_is_the_pages_asked_for_and_zero_is_one`.

The defect: a zero count passed through as zero rather than meaning one page. Every caller before
the count existed passed 0, so this would turn every existing single-page `RETYPE` into a refused
empty carve, and the tree would stop being able to mint a frame at all.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(watermark.checked_add(want).is_none() || watermark + want >
pages, "a run that fits must not be refused")`, at `requested == 0` with room left, which the
defect refuses because `split_new_watermark` refuses an empty carve.

diff --git a/crates/memory_regions/src/lib.rs b/crates/memory_regions/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/memory_regions/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/memory_regions/src/lib.rs
@@ -84,3 +84,3 @@ pub const fn retype_pages(requested: u64) -> u64 {
 pub const fn retype_pages(requested: u64) -> u64 {
-    if requested == 0 { 1 } else { requested }
+    requested
 }
